PpmiFicCrossTenantFailed.message:
Could not configure the federated identity credential automatically.

Reason: cross-tenant access failed.
  - Authenticated tenant: {0}
  - Managed identity tenant: {1}
  - App registration '{2}' not accessible in either tenant

Manual FIC values to create in Azure Portal (under app registration {2} > Certificates & secrets > Federated credentials):
  Issuer:   {3}
  Subject:  {4}
  Audience: {5}

Fix options:
  1. Re-authenticate to the MI's tenant and retry:
     pac auth create --tenant {1}
  2. Or have a tenant admin grant your account 'Application.ReadWrite.OwnedBy' (or higher) on app registration {2} in tenant {1}.
  3. Or create the federated identity credential manually in Azure Portal with the Issuer/Subject/Audience above, then re-run this command.

PpmiUpgradeManualFicRequired.message:
Unable to automatically configure the federated identity credential for {0} ({1}) because Azure access is not available. Please manually create the federated identity credential with the following values:

Issuer: {2}
Subject: {3}
Audience: {4}

After creating the credential in Azure Portal, re-run the upgrade command.

